Horizon: let the libretro core enable Azahar's asynchronous shader compilation.

Azahar 2126.2 implements async_shader_compilation (Vulkan pipelines are built
on worker threads instead of stalling the frame) and its Qt and Android
frontends expose it, but the libretro core never reads it. This adds a
citra_async_shader_compilation core option (default disabled, as upstream) and
applies it with the other graphics options. Horizon sets it to enabled.

Modified 2026-10-24 for Horizon. GPL-2.0-or-later, as the rest of Azahar.

